{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL Injection vulnerability in order cancellation reason","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The cancel_reason value from the request JSON is interpolated directly into the SQL query string using an f-string instead of using a parameterized query. This allows an attacker to perform SQL injection attacks by supplying malicious input in the 'reason' field.","suggested_fix":"Use a parameterized query for the cancel_reason, e.g., db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]},{"id":"F2","title":"Missing authorization check for order ownership","category":"security","severity":"high","confidence":"medium","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":45,"end_line":47},"explanation":"Although @require_login is used and current_user(request) is called, the code does not verify whether the currently authenticated user actually owns the order being cancelled. Any logged-in user can cancel any other user's order by guessing or iterating order IDs.","suggested_fix":"Verify that the order belongs to the currently authenticated user before allowing cancellation.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"},{"finding_id":"F2","issue_id":"idor","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1144,"output_tokens":399,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":1,"cached_requests":0,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":17.726,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL Injection vulnerability in cancel reason update","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The 'reason' variable obtained from the request JSON is directly interpolated into the SQL query string using f-strings. This allows an attacker to perform SQL injection attacks by supplying malicious input in the 'reason' field.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries for the cancel_reason as well, e.g., \"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\" with parameters (reason, int(order_id)).","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1144,"output_tokens":231,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":1,"cached_requests":0,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":15.834,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Missing check for whether the user exists during role update","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":33},"explanation":"The UPDATE query executes directly without checking if any rows were matched or updated. If a non-existent user ID is provided, the endpoint still returns a 204 No Content response and attempts to fetch/email a user that does not exist.","suggested_fix":"Check the number of affected rows or verify the user exists before sending notifications, similar to the deactivate_user endpoint.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"unvalidated-role","distance":2,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1239,"output_tokens":218,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":1,"cached_requests":0,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":6.04,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Missing check if user exists when updating role","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":33},"explanation":"The endpoint executes an UPDATE query without checking if any rows were actually changed (unlike deactivate_user above which checks for changed == 0 and raises a 404). If an invalid or non-existent user_id is provided, the endpoint returns a 204 No Content response as if it succeeded.","suggested_fix":"Check the number of changed rows or verify the user exists before returning a success response.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"unvalidated-role","distance":2,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1239,"output_tokens":222,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":1,"cached_requests":0,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":16.819,"error":null}
