{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-uuid-converter","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Overly permissive regex allows invalid UUID string formats","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":245,"end_line":245},"explanation":"The regex `[A-Fa-f0-9-]{32,36}` matches strings consisting of 32 to 36 hex digits and hyphens in any position or combination, which accepts malformed strings like `------------------------------------` or misplaced dashes that are not valid UUIDs. While `uuid.UUID(value)` will subsequently raise an exception for truly invalid UUIDs, route matching will capture these malformed strings and cause 500 server errors or unexpected routing behavior instead of a 404 Not Found.","suggested_fix":"Use a regex that explicitly matches either the 32-character hex string or the standard hyphenated format, such as `r'[A-Fa-f0-9]{32}|[A-Fa-f0-9]{8}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{4}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{4}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{4}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{12}'`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"uncaught-value-error","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":886,"output_tokens":364,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":1,"cached_requests":1,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":0.003,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-uuid-converter","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Overly permissive regex in UUIDConverter allows invalid UUID formats","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":245,"end_line":245},"explanation":"The regex `[A-Fa-f0-9-]{32,36}` matches any combination of hex characters and hyphens between 32 and 36 characters long. This incorrectly matches strings with misplaced hyphens, multiple consecutive hyphens, or entirely wrong structures (like 36 hyphens), which will then fail when passed to `uuid.UUID(value)` in `to_python` and raise an unexpected 500 or ValueError instead of a 404 route mismatch.","suggested_fix":"Use a regex that correctly alternates between standard and compact UUID patterns, such as `r'[A-Fa-f0-9]{32}|[A-Fa-f0-9]{8}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{4}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{4}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{4}-[A-Fa-f0-9]{12}'`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"uncaught-value-error","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":886,"output_tokens":341,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":1,"cached_requests":1,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":0.002,"error":null}
